{
  "_comment": [
    "The tool verifying itself. Each mutation is a way mutation-check.py could",
    "manufacture false confidence, and each names the test that must catch it:",
    "  scripts/mutation-check.py run scripts/mutation-check-self-spec.json",
    "",
    "Requires a clean tree (the tool refuses otherwise) and mutates the tool's own",
    "source, which is why invalidate_pycache() exists -- without it a mutation could",
    "report the PREVIOUS mutation's failure signature."
  ],
  "runner": "unittest",
  "cwd": ".",
  "command": [
    "python3",
    "-m",
    "unittest",
    "discover",
    "-s",
    "scripts",
    "-p",
    "test_mutation_check.py"
  ],
  "baseline_tests": 88,
  "mutations": [
